
### POST /api/events/{topic}
# Records an event. 200 + summary if the topic is approved and public, otherwise 204.
# X-Real-IP is normally set by nginx; locally it must be sent by hand.

@topic = reactions

### Toggle reaction on
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/dev-test
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "resourceUrl": "/blog/hello",
  "visitorId": "visitor-1",
  "data": {
    "type": "like",
    "active": true
  }
}

### Toggle reaction off (sends state, not a click: repeating it changes nothing)
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/{{topic}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "resourceUrl": "/blog/hello",
  "visitorId": "visitor-1",
  "data": { "type": "like", "active": false }
}

### Resource by id and url (preferred: send both, the same way every time)
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/{{topic}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "resourceId": "post:123",
  "resourceUrl": "/blog/hello",
  "visitorId": "visitor-2",
  "data": { "type": "fire" }
}

### Append-style feedback form
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "resourceUrl": "/contact",
  "visitorId": "visitor-1",
  "data": { "message": "Nice site!", "email": "me@example.com" },
  "website": ""
}

### Honeypot filled -> 204, nothing stored
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "resourceUrl": "/contact",
  "visitorId": "bot",
  "data": { "message": "spam" },
  "website": "http://spam.example"
}

### Missing resource -> 400
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/{{topic}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

{
  "visitorId": "visitor-1",
  "data": { "type": "like" }
}

### Wrong content type -> 415
POST {{publicUrl}}/api/events/{{topic}}
Content-Type: text/plain
X-Real-IP: 127.0.0.1

hello
